---
# `safety`, not `production`: this workflow is internal automation for one repo,
# not a shared/published role. `production` additionally enforces two purely
# cosmetic style rules we deliberately don't follow, for stated reasons:
#   - name[template]: would force every task name's Jinja to the end
#     ("Check X for {{ cluster.name }}"). This role instead leads every task
#     name with "{{ cluster.name }}: ..." on purpose, so ansible-playbook's
#     per-task output is scannable by cluster when multiple clusters run in
#     one invocation (the actual multi-cluster design goal, correction #2).
#   - var-naming[no-role-prefix]: would require every internal fact to be
#     prefixed `onprem_cluster_onboarding_...`. This role instead uses a
#     leading underscore (`_gcloud_auth`, `_rbac_apply`, ...) for role-private
#     facts, which is Ansible's own documented convention for "these are
#     internal, don't rely on them from outside this role."
# All `safety`-tier rules (idempotency, no-changed-when gaps, real correctness
# checks) still apply and must pass clean.
profile: safety
skip_list:
  - yaml[line-length]
  - name[template]
  - var-naming[no-role-prefix]
